# Docker / Prisma / Auth Rules

## Docker
- Base image: `node:20-bookworm-slim` (not Alpine; Prisma needs OpenSSL).
- Runner must install openssl: `RUN apt-get update -y && apt-get install -y openssl`.
- Startup CMD order: `prisma db push` -> `seed` -> `node server.js`.
- Call Prisma CLI via `node node_modules/prisma/build/index.js` (npx unavailable in slim runner).
- Ports: db `5433:5432`, app `3001:3000` (avoid conflict with other local services).

## Prisma
- After any schema change: `npx prisma generate` locally, rebuild Docker image.
- Prefer `--skip-generate` in container CMD since generate ran at build time.
- Use `@@unique`, `@@index` for composite lookups; avoid full-table scans.
- Keep `select/include` minimal in queries.

## Auth (NextAuth v5 / Auth.js)
- Set both `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` and `AUTH_SECRET` in Docker env for compatibility.
- Always set `secret` explicitly in NextAuth config: `process.env.NEXTAUTH_SECRET || process.env.AUTH_SECRET`.
- `trustHost: true` required when running behind Docker/proxy.
- Credentials provider: bcrypt compare, return `role` in JWT callback.
- Middleware protects `/dashboard` (login required) and `/admin` (ADMIN role required).
- Seed script creates admin `admin@example.com` / `Admin@123` on first run.